== Implementation ==
backend/app/security.py: pages_preview_projects() derives https://<project>.pages.dev projects from
  CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (plus CORS_ALLOW_PAGES_PREVIEWS); allowed_origin_regex() adds
  ^https://[a-z0-9-]+\.<project>\.pages\.dev$ for each; is_allowed_origin() applies the CORS middleware's two rules
  (exact list, fullmatch of the regex); PublicHealthCorsMiddleware, outermost, answers OPTIONS /health with 204 and *
  and adds Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * to /health responses; every other path passes through untouched.
  cors_summary() reports pages_preview_projects and the public path.
backend/app/models.py HealthResponse: commit, commit_short, data, origin_allowed.
backend/app/main.py /health: build_commit(), knowledge_identity() (B2's, cached), origin_allowed for the request's
  Origin (null without one); the middleware is added last, so outermost.
app/lib/api/pharmaguard_api.dart: healthCheck() replaces health(): 10 s receive timeout on every platform;
  outcomes ready / blocked (origin_allowed false) / noAnswer (DioException, 502/503/504) / serverError (other
  status, or a 200 without ok). ApiException.kind: declined (4xx with an error code), serverError (5xx, other
  4xx), network (no status), busy, rateLimited.
app/lib/models/analysis.dart: HealthReport (reads every HealthResponse field; HealthResponse joins the parity list).
app/lib/api/backend_status.dart: phases blocked and serverError, each terminal after one ping; noAnswer keeps
  waking; budget carried on BackendStatus (budgetFraction, secondsLeft); the give-up message says there was no
  answer (and names a gateway status when the host's gateway answered), never "responded but did not report
  healthy".
app/lib/widgets/backend_status_banner.dart: the bar is elapsed / budget (was / 90 s); the line under it gives the
  seconds left of the budget; blocked and serverError get their own icons and a retry button.
app/lib/widgets/error_panel.dart (new): ErrorPanel with a heading per ApiErrorKind; home_screen.dart uses it and
  records e.kind for both the preview and the analysis; the analysing copy says "about a minute" and that a queued
  request waits for the running one (was "roughly 50–60 seconds", under the 58–68 s measured live on 2026-11-05).
app/lib/config.dart kColdStartExpectation: "usually 20–30 seconds, occasionally longer if the server image has to
  be fetched again" (measured 22.40 s, 22.45 s in B4; 28.4 s end to end in B6).
Docs: README.md, docs/DEMO_SCRIPT.md (two places), infra/DEPLOY_NOTES.md quote B4's 22.40 s / 22.45 s; the old
  figures stay only as labelled history. reports/deployment_verification.md keeps its original reading under a
  dated "Superseded" note. git grep "12.85" outside audit/: only history-labelled lines remain (README, config.dart
  and backend_status_test comments, DEPLOY_NOTES, the superseded report). DEPLOY_NOTES and backend/.env.example
  describe the derived preview origins.
scripts/scientific_hash_policy.json: app/lib/widgets/error_panel.dart enrolled (95 core paths).

== Existing tests changed, each because the planned behaviour changed ==
- app/test/backend_status_test.dart: the fake now scripts healthCheck(); true/false keep their meaning (false =
  no answer yet). Eight new tests: blocked, server error, gateway-then-ready, no "responded" on give-up, six distinct
  headlines, the bar at 90 s of 180 s is 0.5, never full, an injected budget is the one used.
- app/test/state_census_test.dart: BackendPhase count 4 -> 6 (both new phases render at 360 px in the existing
  per-phase loop).
- app/test/wait_states_test.dart: header figures updated to B4's measurements (comment only).
- backend/tests/test_deployment.py: the CORS allowlist tests asked /health; since /health answers every origin by
  design they now ask `/`. test_health_is_dependency_free checks status and keys instead of the old exact body.
- backend/tests/test_analyze_api.py test_health: status only (test_public_health.py pins the rest).
- backend/tests/test_build_identity.py test_health_stays_trivial: its rule ("keep the probe cheap") is kept and made
  checkable: no subprocess of any kind, and the jar is not re-read after the first call (knowledge_identity cache).
New: backend/tests/test_public_health.py (26, by pytest --collect-only), app/test/connectivity_states_test.dart (20, including two banner widget tests added for AC3's countdown).

== Sabotage (audit/phase9/partb/b7_sabotage.py -> B7.sabotage.stdout; every file restored identical) ==
SB7-a /health stops adding *                2 red.
SB7-b preview regex loses ^ and $ (planned)  0 red. Not a weakening: Starlette 0.49.3's CORSMiddleware checks the
                                             regex with fullmatch, and so does is_allowed_origin, so the anchors
                                             change nothing. Reported as planned, not hidden. The plan's sabotage
                                             was wrong for this code.
SB7-b2 preview label may contain dots       1 red (a.b.pharmaguard-web.pages.dev accepted): a real loosening, caught.
SB7-c * on every path                       7 red.
SB7-d origin_allowed false read as ready    1 red. (First attempt stopped on the pre-format text of the line; the
                                             target was corrected to the formatted source and the three client
                                             sabotages rerun.)
SB7-e the bar divides by 90 s again         2 red.
SB7-f a declined 400 maps to server error   1 red.

